# START — Agent Entry Gate & Routing Specification
Floor: 2
Thrust: 9
Patch: 3
File: openOODA/START.oot

Operate within this directory. All relative paths start from this directory.

## 0. The 10 Strategic Governance Pillars & Core Laws

1. Pillar 1 (First Principles & Pure File Extension Laws): Pure .oo (code) and .oot (docs). Prohibit .py, .sh, .js, .md in product scope. Derive from IEEE 754, NIST KATs, RFCs. Reject incomplete stubs.
2. Pillar 2 (Boyd's E-M Invariant & Zero Drag): Ps = ((T - D) / W) * V. Maximize emission speed, eliminate GC/drag, minimize context/token weight. Strict <= 256 lines per file. Zero intermediate artifacts in std/.
3. Pillar 3 (Adversarial Validation & Double-Run Invariant): Negative trust: assume unverified code is defective. Multi-agent teams must deploy the 8-Dimensional Red Team (Red 1..Red 8) with blocking veto power (see REDTEAM.oot):
   - Red 1 (Heuristic Hunter / e1): Probes lowering to reject token/string bag-of-words heuristics.
   - Red 2 (Boundary Falsifier / e2): Probes validators with dynamic oversized inputs (e.g. head_dim = 512).
   - Red 3 (Data-Path Tracer / e3): Rejects (void)code and silent fallback routing.
   - Red 4 (Hermetic Jailor / e4): Rejects out-of-tree escapes and unauthorized ambient authority.
   - Red 5 (Temporal Saboteur / e5): Probes concurrency races, stream synchronization, and replay drift.
   - Red 6 (Drag Assassin / e6): Probes super-linear scaling, memory leaks, and GC pause latency.
   - Red 7 (Semantic Subverter / e7): Probes AST mutant survival (kill rate >= 95%) and vacuous contracts.
   - Red 8 (Byzantine Infiltrator / e8): Probes timing side channels (|t_Welch| < 4.5) and RASP rollback.
4. Pillar 4 (Academy 4-Element Headers): Mandatory ASD-STE100 headers (# Title, Logline, Setup, Beats on .oo; Title, Floor, Thrust, Patch, File on .oot).
5. Pillar 5 (Capability Security & Zero Ambient Authority): Zero ambient authority with 14 unforgeable capability tokens (&FsReadCap, &FsWriteCap, &ProcessCap, &NetCap, &SysCap, etc.).
6. Pillar 6 (Multi-Agent Swarm Safety & Topology Invariance): Autonomous swarms operate on stationary workspace topology (Delta_path = 0). Agent fork bombs and identity mutations fail closed.
7. Pillar 7 (Formal RFC Template Compliance): All RFCs in openOODA/rfcs/ must comply with 0000-template.oot (RFC ID, Author, Status, Security, Testing).
8. Pillar 8 (Two-Binary Architecture): Decoupled compiler (oodac) and workflow driver (ooda). Compiler handles SSA lowering; driver coordinates workflows.
9. Pillar 9 (Gen 1 C/H Substrate Isolation): Low-level C runtime shims (chs_rt_*.c, chs_rt.h) strictly confined to ooda/runtime/. Zero C header leaks into ooda/std/.
10. Pillar 10 (Zero Loose Unheaded Files & Clean Workspaces): Zero loose unheaded .oo files in roots, zero struct trailing commas, clean workspace.
11. Law 11 (Hard Engineering): Build real AST pipelines. Decompose across modular files (<= 256 lines). Break-test first.
12. Law 12 (Generational SemVer): v<Floor>.<Thrust>.<Patch>. Verified state: v2.9.3 from ooda.pkg.

