## 2. Reading Priority (Token-Optimized)
- Sovereign Agent Ingress: Read LLMS.oot first for immediate orientation, syntax laws, and OCap tokens.
- Always Read: User request, START.oot, RULES.oot, SHIPPED.oot, SECURITY.oot §1-2, WORKFLOW.oot §0.
- When Coding: ROADMAP.oot, target RFC, CONSTRAINTS.oot, REDTEAM.oot.
- Only as Needed: FORMAT.oot (headers), QUICKREF.oot (syntax), MOONSHOTS.oot (specs), STRUCTURE_EM.oot.

## 3. Pre-Modification & Completion Gate
Before modifying product code, declare:
1. Active Goal (ROADMAP milestone).
2. Governing Axiom (RULES.oot principle).
3. Adversarial Break-Test (hostile probe that fails closed on current code).
Before claiming victory: Execute all 8 Red Team falsification probes live (per 8-Gate Blocking Veto Protocol in REDTEAM.oot). If any defect, facade, or fallback is found, victory is vetoed.
